        "authority": "CITES Secretariat (CITES)",
        "iucn": 5,
        "url": "",
        "description": "Precautionary location protection applied to limit dissemination of precise coordinates for a location-sensitive taxon potentially vulnerable to harvesting and illegal trade. All native orchid species are legally protected from international trade by listing under CITES Appendix II. Large scale wild harvesting (e.g., for salep production) has been documented as a pressure on certain populations in some Greek regions. This designation is intended as a risk-reduction measure only and does not represent a formal conservation assessment.",
